    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

    <h3>Are slim pouches actually discreet enough for work?</h3>
    <p>Yes. A slim pouch sits between your gum and lip without creating any visible bulge. Most people won't notice you're wearing one. The pouch is completely silent. The slim format also reduces oral irritation risk by approximately 20%, with lower contact time on gum tissue translating to better tolerance in long-session users (<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23732784/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Perfetti &amp; Caggiula (2013)</a>).</p>

    <h3>How long does a slim pouch last?</h3>
    <p>Most slim pouches remain effective for 30–60 minutes. Premium brands like ZYN and VELO tend toward the longer end.</p>

    <h3>Is slim format suitable for beginners?</h3>
    <p>Absolutely. Start with a light-strength slim pouch (4–6mg). The slim format's faster nicotine release and smaller size make it ideal for newcomers.</p>

    <h3>What's the difference between slim and mini pouches?</h3>
    <p>Mini pouches (0.3–0.4g) are lighter and nearly invisible—ideal for maximum discretion. Slim pouches (0.5–0.6g) provide a longer-lasting experience. For regular users, slim is the better balance. Slim is also 5x more available (672 vs. 52 products).</p>

    <h3>Why are budget slim pouches so cheap?</h3>
    <p>Budget slim pouches are cheaper not because they're low quality, but because they're produced in higher volumes and sold with minimal branding. Quality remains solid—you're just buying less brand prestige.</p>

